# Project Architecture

Electron 37 + electron-vite 4 + React 19 + Tailwind 4 desktop app for SSHR database backup, restore, and migrate. All CLI orchestration runs in TypeScript in the main process — no shell scripts.

## File index

| Task | Start here |
|------|------------|
| New job type / CLI work | `src/main/jobs.ts` + domain module (`migrate.ts`, `databases.ts`, `process.ts`) |
| IPC channel | `src/main/index.ts` → `src/preload/index.ts` |
| Shared types / constants | `src/shared/types.ts` |
| New screen | `src/renderer/src/pages/*Page.tsx` + route in `App.tsx` |
| Reusable UI | `src/renderer/src/components/ui.tsx` |
| Status / logs UX | `LogConsole.tsx` + `src/renderer/src/lib/logFormat.ts` |
| Settings persistence | `src/main/settings.ts` |
| Readiness scan | `src/main/readiness.ts` |
| Packaged paths | `src/main/paths.ts` |
| Build / installers | `package.json` `build` field; run `pnpm dist:linux` |

## Process boundaries

- **main** — spawn, fs, settings, dialogs, all side effects
- **preload** — `contextBridge` → `window.api` only
- **renderer** — React UI; calls `window.api`, never Node/Electron APIs
- **shared** — types and constants imported by all three

## Hard rules

- One active job at a time (`src/main/jobs.ts`)
- Passwords in job input only — never persist in `settings.json`
- Destructive restore requires typed `RECREATE` or `DROP`
- Validate database names before SQL
- Use relative imports to shared types (match existing code; `@shared`/`@renderer` aliases exist but are unused — do not mix styles in one change)
